  <main id="main-content">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px 56px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 56px; align-items: center" aria-labelledby="l2-s1">
      <div style="flex: 1 1 480px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px 16px"><a href="#new" class="l2-tag l2-tag--pink">New in 2.0: our own voices</a><span style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #A3A3A0">Text to speech reader for iPhone and iPad</span></div>
        <h1 id="l2-s1" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 76px); line-height: 1.02; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.03em">Listen to the <span style="background: #006E99; border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 6px">reading</span> you keep putting off.</h1>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 21px); line-height: 1.55; color: #D4D4D0; max-width: 620px">Listen2 turns your PDFs, books and saved articles into audiobooks: a natural voice reads them aloud and each word is highlighted as it is spoken. Version 2.0 adds {{ listen2Voices.voiceCount }} English voices that we trained ourselves, from the ground up, and they come with the app, so you can press play as soon as it is installed. Every voice runs on your iPhone itself, so Listen2 keeps working on a plane or in the mountains, and nothing you read is sent to us.</p>
        <div class="l2-hero-ctas" style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; align-items: center">
          <a id="download" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/listen-2-reader/id6755753624" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 56px; padding: 0 28px; border-radius: 28px; background: #FF751F; color: #111113; font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; text-decoration: none">Download on the App Store</a>
          <a href="#voices" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 56px; padding: 0 26px; border-radius: 28px; border: 2px solid #38B6FF; color: #38B6FF; font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; text-decoration: none">Hear the voices</a>
        </div>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">Free for 7 days, then a single purchase of $24.99. No subscription.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="flex: 0 1 340px; margin: 0 auto">
        <div style="width: 100%; max-width: 340px; aspect-ratio: 590 / 1278; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 10px; border-radius: 54px; background: #1C1C1E; border: 1px solid #3A3A3D">
          <video src="/assets/listen2/web/hero-reader.mp4" poster="/assets/listen2/web/hero-reader-poster.jpg" autoplay="" muted loop="" playsinline="" controls="" aria-label="Listen2 reading a chapter aloud on iPhone, with each spoken word highlighted in blue" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 44px; background: #000000"><track kind="captions" src="/assets/listen2/web/hero-reader.vtt" srclang="en" label="English"></video>
        </div>
        <p style="margin: 12px 0 0; text-align: center; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">Tap the video to hear the voice.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {% include "components/listen2-2/whats-new.njk" %}

    <!-- Problem -->
    <section style="background: #131315; border-top: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-bottom: 1px solid #2A2A2D" aria-labelledby="l2-s2">
      <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px">
        <div style="max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
          <h2 id="l2-s2" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Most reading apps make you pick two out of three</h2>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">If you wanted voices that sound human, you usually paid a monthly subscription and sent your documents to someone's server. If you wanted to stay offline, you got the robotic system voices. And if you wanted to follow along on the page, most apps could only do that with Apple's own voices. Listen2 was built so you would not have to give any of that up.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 16px">
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; background: #0B0B0C">
            <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #7ED957"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">It works offline</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Every voice runs on your iPhone, and the 25 Phonon voices are there from the first launch. You do not need an account, and nothing you read is sent to us.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; background: #0B0B0C">
            <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF66C4"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">The voices are neural</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">{{ listen2Voices.voiceCount }} Listen2 Voices of our own, 25 from Phonon and 10 from Supertonic, which reads 13 languages. Apple's Premium voices are there too.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; background: #0B0B0C">
            <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FFCC00"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">Every word is highlighted</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">The neural voices get word-by-word highlighting too, the same as Apple's voices do.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; background: #0B0B0C">
            <div style="width: 40px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF751F"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700">You pay once</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">One purchase unlocks the whole app. There is nothing to renew and nothing metered by the hour.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who listens -->
    <section style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px" aria-labelledby="l2-s3">
      <div style="max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <h2 id="l2-s3" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 3.5vw, 42px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Who listens with it</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">Listen2 started with blind and low-vision readers, and they still shape most of what changes in it. More and more of the people writing in can see the page perfectly well. They just have more to read than time to sit and read it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 16px">
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
            <div style="width: 32px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #7ED957"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700">People who read with VoiceOver</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Blind and low-vision readers use it every day, and much of the app was built from their emails, down to how the rotor moves through a sentence.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
            <div style="width: 32px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF751F"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700">Anyone whose hands are busy</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">A commute, a walk or a sink full of dishes becomes reading time. Lock the phone and the chapter keeps going.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
            <div style="width: 32px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #38B6FF"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700">Students and researchers</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Two-column papers are read in the right order and footnotes can be skipped, so a reading list can be worked through on the way to class.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
            <div style="width: 32px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FFCC00"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700">Readers who lose their place</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">If long pages are slow going or your attention drifts, seeing each word while you hear it gives you something to hold on to.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 20px; padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
            <div style="width: 32px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: #FF66C4"></div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700">Language learners</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: #A3A3A0">Thirteen languages are fully supported, so you can hear how a sentence in Spanish or German sounds while you follow it word by word.</p>
          </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Highlight -->
    <section id="highlight" style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 56px; align-items: center" aria-labelledby="l2-s4">
      <div style="flex: 1 1 460px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
        <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #FFCC00">Word-level highlighting</div>
        <h2 id="l2-s4" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Your eyes and your ears stay on the same word</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">When you only listen, it is easy to drift for a paragraph and lose the thread. Seeing each word as you hear it gives your attention something to hold on to, and if you look away, you can find your place again in a glance.</p>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #A3A3A0">You can highlight by word or by sentence and add a soft band on the current line. The page scrolls with you, or it can keep the current line in the middle of the screen like a teleprompter. In light mode the word sits on yellow; in dark mode it sits on blue, and the text itself never changes color.</p>
        <blockquote style="margin: 8px 0 0; display: flex; gap: 18px">
          <div style="width: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: #FF751F; flex-shrink: 0"></div>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.45">"After trying about 30 apps this one has the voices and smooth reading that I was looking for."</p>
            <cite style="font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">App Store review, United States, 5 stars</cite>
          </div>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
          <video controls="" src="/assets/listen2/web/header-loop.mp4" poster="/assets/listen2/web/header-loop-poster.jpg" autoplay="" muted loop="" playsinline="" aria-label="Alice in Wonderland being read aloud, with the highlight moving from word to word" style="display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1920 / 824; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 24px; border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; background: #000000"></video>
          <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/listen2/web/ipad-reader.webp" alt="Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, A Mad Tea-Party, playing on iPad with the spoken word highlighted" style="display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 24px; border: 1px solid #2A2A2D">
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Voices -->
    <section id="voices" style="background: #131315; border-top: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-bottom: 1px solid #2A2A2D" aria-labelledby="l2-s5">
      <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px; align-items: flex-end">
          <div style="flex: 1 1 520px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
            <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #FF66C4">Voices</div>
            <h2 id="l2-s5" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Voices that sound like people, running on your phone</h2>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">Listen2 runs three neural voice engines on your iPhone. The newest is our own: {{ listen2Voices.voiceCount }} English voices that we trained ourselves, new in 2.0. They come with the app, so they work the first time you open it, on every device Listen2 supports. Phonon, from Gradium, has 25 English voices with American and British accents, and they are a free download. Supertonic has 10 voices, and each one can read all 13 of Listen2's languages, so the same voice can take you from an English novel to a German newspaper. Each is a single download, and after that it works anywhere too.</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #A3A3A0">Apple's Premium and Enhanced voices are built in as well. They are reliable, they cover nearly every language, and Listen2 highlights them word by word like the others. If you have made your own voice with Supertone's Voice Builder, you can import it and read with it.</p>
