    <!-- Import -->
    <section style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap-reverse; gap: 56px; align-items: center" aria-labelledby="l2-s6">
      <div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0">
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap">
          <div style="flex: 0 0 auto; width: 240px; max-width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1320 / 2868; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 9px; border-radius: 48px; background: #1C1C1E; border: 1px solid #3A3A3D"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/listen2/web/safari-share.webp" alt="Safari's share sheet on a web article, with Listen2 in the row of apps" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 40px"></div>
          <div style="position: relative; width: 260px; max-width: 100%">
            <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/listen2/web/paper-page.webp" alt="The first page of a two-column research paper" style="display: block; width: 170px; aspect-ratio: 200 / 260; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; background: #FFFFFF; border-radius: 6px; transform: rotate(-4deg); margin: 0 0 -60px -10px; position: relative; z-index: 0">
            <div style="position: relative; z-index: 1; margin-left: 30px"><div style="flex: 0 0 auto; width: 230px; max-width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1320 / 2868; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 9px; border-radius: 48px; background: #1C1C1E; border: 1px solid #3A3A3D"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/listen2/web/paper-reader.webp" alt="The research paper's abstract in the Listen2 reader, with the spoken word highlighted" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 40px"></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="flex: 1 1 460px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
        <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #38B6FF">Import</div>
        <h2 id="l2-s6" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Bring in whatever you are reading</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">Open PDFs, EPUBs, Word documents, DAISY books, Markdown and plain text from Files, iCloud Drive, Dropbox or Google Drive. To listen to an article, share it from Safari, and Listen2 leaves the ads and menus behind. You can also paste text, import a link, or ask Siri to read what is on your clipboard.</p>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #A3A3A0">PDFs are the hard case, so Listen2 does extra work on them. It reads multi-column pages in the right order, rejoins words split by hyphens, and can skip footnotes and citation brackets. If a PDF is only scanned images, Listen2 notices and offers to recognize the text on your device.</p>
        <blockquote style="margin: 8px 0 0; display: flex; gap: 18px">
          <div style="width: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: #FF751F; flex-shrink: 0"></div>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.45">"Thank you! Thank you! Thank you! ... With this app I have CHAPTER TITLES again!"</p>
            <cite style="font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">App Store review, United States, after struggling with PDFs elsewhere</cite>
          </div>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Figure descriptions -->
    <section style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px 88px" aria-labelledby="l2-s7">
      <div style="border: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-radius: 28px; background: #131315; padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px; align-items: center">
        <div style="flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
          <h2 id="l2-s7" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 36px); line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 700">It describes the pictures, too</h2>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">Charts and photos usually get skipped when a document is read aloud. Listen2 can download a small image model, about 350 MB, that writes a short description of each figure on your phone and reads it at the point where the figure appears. While it reads, you can look at the picture itself or follow the description as text, and you choose brief or standard detail.</p>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; color: #A3A3A0">The descriptions are written by a model on your phone, so they can get details wrong, and Listen2 says so on screen.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1 1 320px; min-width: 0">
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; justify-content: center"><div style="flex: 0 1 220px; min-width: 0; aspect-ratio: 1290 / 2796; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px; border-radius: 44px; background: #1C1C1E; border: 1px solid #3A3A3D"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/listen2/web/figure-image.webp" alt="The cover illustration of Alice in Wonderland shown full screen while Listen2 reads its description" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 36px"></div><div style="flex: 0 1 220px; min-width: 0; aspect-ratio: 1290 / 2796; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px; border-radius: 44px; background: #1C1C1E; border: 1px solid #3A3A3D"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/listen2/web/figure-description.webp" alt="The written description of the Alice in Wonderland cover, with play controls and a note that it is AI-generated" style="display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 36px"></div></div>
        </div>
