    <!-- Accessibility -->
    <section id="accessibility" style="background: #131315; border-top: 1px solid #2A2A2D; border-bottom: 1px solid #2A2A2D" aria-labelledby="l2-s8">
      <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 48px">
          <div style="flex: 1 1 520px; min-width: 0; max-width: 820px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
            <div style="font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #7ED957">Accessibility</div>
            <h2 id="l2-s8" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Shaped by the blind and low-vision people who use it</h2>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; color: #D4D4D0">Many of the people who read with Listen2 every day use VoiceOver, and a good part of the app was designed around their emails. You can move through a document by sentence, line, paragraph or heading with the rotor, use Magic Tap to play and pause, and hear where you are without fighting the interface.</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #A3A3A0">For readers with low vision or dyslexia, there are 13 reading fonts, including Atkinson Hyperlegible and OpenDyslexic, along with control over text size, line spacing, letter spacing and line length. The app follows your system text size if you prefer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 24px">
          <blockquote style="margin: 0; display: flex; gap: 18px">
            <div style="width: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: #FF751F; flex-shrink: 0"></div>
            <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.5">"It is 100% accessible with VoiceOver. The app comes with a vast number of neural TTS voices of exceptional quality and the amazing thing is that they work offline!"</p>
              <cite style="font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">App Store review, South Africa, 5 stars</cite>
            </div>
          </blockquote>
          <blockquote style="margin: 0; display: flex; gap: 18px">
            <div style="width: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: #FF751F; flex-shrink: 0"></div>
            <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.5">"As a blind user, finding an app that integrates so well with VoiceOver and offers high-quality neural voices locally is a game-changer."</p>
              <cite style="font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">VoiceOver user</cite>
            </div>
          </blockquote>
          <blockquote style="margin: 0; display: flex; gap: 18px">
            <div style="width: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: #FF751F; flex-shrink: 0"></div>
            <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.5">"I can't express how delighted I am that you support navigation by sentence instead of by line."</p>
              <cite style="font-style: normal; font-size: 15px; color: #A3A3A0">Listen2 reader</cite>
            </div>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
